Here’s how to list GCP’s manual snapshots. projectIds.txt contains a list of projects.
#!/bin/bash ts=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S) log=&#34;manual-snapshots-logs-$ts&#34; &gt;$log while read -r project; do snapshots=$(gcloud compute snapshots list \ --project $project \ --filter=&#34;sourceSnapshotSchedulePolicy!=&#39;&#39;&#34; \ --format=&#34;value(name)&#34;) for snapshot in $snapshots do printf &#34;%-30s %-30s \n&#34; &#34;$project&#34; &#34;$snapshot&#34; | tee -a $log done done &gt; projectIds.txt Another option.
